  "summary": "A distinctive fortress-temple architecture characterized by massive walls, inward-sloping walls, and courtyards that serve both administrative and religious functions.",
  "description": "Dzongs feature thick, whitewashed walls with upward-leaning windows, steep roofs extending beyond walls, and intricate woodwork. This defensive yet elegant design reflects both the need for protection and the spiritual importance of these administrative centers.",
